      "message": "[error] Line 586: 🔴 `returnToCall()` currently calls `requestRestore()`, but `requestRestore()` bails out unless `pipState \u003d\u003d .minimized`. In both fallback paths (`minimizeToReturnCapsule()` and `fallBackToReturnCapsule()`), `pipState` is left/set to `.inactive`, so tapping the return capsule becomes a no-op and users can be stranded outside the call UI. Fix by making capsule restore independent of PiP state (e.g., call `onRestore` directly from `returnToCall()`), or keep a dedicated minimized-via-capsule state that passes the restore guard.",
